name issue_76_rtx_v2_keyframe_flush
describe RTX history with the pacer keyframe flush: a resend flushed by a keyframe must not stay pending (#76 group 2, review of PR #97)
# NACKed packets are queued as resends; PacingController discards them when a keyframe starts.
# The history must hear about it (RtpSender::OnPacketDropped), else the packet stays pending.
pacer v2
keyframe v2
rtx v2
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=400ms loss=2%
at 10s capacity=500kbps
at 25s capacity=2500kbps
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 4000
expect video.residual_loss_pct < 1
